What is BCD Process Technology?
BCD (Bipolar-CMOS-DMOS) is an advanced semiconductor manufacturing process that integrates three distinct technologies on a single chip: Bipolar for analog precision, CMOS for digital control, and DMOS for power handling. This innovative combination enables the creation of power ICs capable of operating at voltages up to 200V while maintaining exceptional energy efficiency.
The technology's ability to embed analog circuits, digital content, power devices, and non-volatile memory (NVM) makes it ideal for power management ICs (PMICs) used in applications ranging from smartphone battery management to electric vehicle motor controllers. This report provides comprehensive insights into the BCD Process Wafer Foundry market, covering everything from macro-level industry trends to micro-level competitive analysis.
